WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.910
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:10.580
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:21.800
break up foreordination

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.680
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.430
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:40.730
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:46.530
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.700
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:56.960
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.500
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.510
wake up your tough intention
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:01.960
wake up your tough intention

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:02.880
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.140
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:13.770
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:15.350
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.820
break up foreordination

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.960
Rematch

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.120
Well?

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.120
Well, what?

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:23.790
I realized you can see the island's testing grounds from here,

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.490
so I thought we should ask if it needed to be sealed off.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:32.800
I can see the pylons, but you can't see the testing ground itself.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.690
There's no need to seal it, Second Lieutenant Nanjou.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.520
I see.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:42.650
Is that all?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.720
It's a nice place.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:52.530
Isn't it?

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:56.830
It's really beautiful, so I wanted to show it to you.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.270
I see.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.190
There are plenty of others, too.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.980
I'll show you the others sometime!

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.060
Ashes to ashes, and dust to dust.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.940
They're pretending the tragedy of Argent Point never happened, huh?

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.120
They could at least put up a plaque.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.150
A town of lies,

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:52.280
which seals away terror that will never fade with bustle and hedonism.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:59.320
That is the one thing humans are good at.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:00.740
It doesn't matter.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:05.640
As long as those who know don't forget, that's enough.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:11.150
If nothing else, I feel better, now that I know you haven't forgotten.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.490
Quasimodo, can you do something for me?

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.200
I want you to find out why the ship was late.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.790
Something's not right.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.650
Sure, that's fine.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.980
Thanks.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:34.450
I can wait, can't I, Marshal?

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.750
I'm a lieutenant now.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:48.460
My sister was here.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.960
Captain Samonji.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.910
What happened with the update to Argevollen?

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.630
After its completion, I got permission from Sergeant Major Suzushiro

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.230
and took Miss Hazaford to the island.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:25.290
I see.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.540
We just happened to find this place on the way back.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:29.810
What about you, Captain?

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.860
A friend told me about it.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.250
A long time ago.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:39.110
I see.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.030
Isn't it a wonderful view?

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:43.770
Private Susumu.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:44.700
Yes, sir.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.100
Tanita and the others will be getting the supplies soon.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.110
Head back to the base and get ready to load up.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:53.010
Yes, sir!

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.130
Incoming message, Major Garp.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:16.280
Okay, tell Battalion 4 to prepare for the attack.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.120
Yes, sir.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.840
Lt. Colonel Holmes, a message from Richthofen.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:25.980
The infiltration was a success.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.320
I see.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.570
Does that upset you?

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.460
Of course it does.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:38.450
That idiot brigadier general, using Richthofen for an operation like this...

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.440
It's senseless.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.870
A full frontal assault combined with

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.060
a surprise attack from the rear to disorient them, is that it?

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:52.350
Even if our advance has stalled,
this is still a bold plan.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:55.150
We drew the short straw, didn't we?

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.190
We'll do our jobs anyway, though.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.280
Are we ready to go?

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.400
Yes, in just a moment.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.780
What are you doing?

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:23.570
What, were you planning on running through town naked?

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.290
Give me a break, Bro.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.690
Don't call me Bro during the mission, Thomas.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:31.620
I apologize, Sergeant Toulouse.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.600
The corporal was correct.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.370
This is camouflage.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:39.520
I've already bought off the customs guards,

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.270
so don't worry.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.110
There were Arandas soldiers in town.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:49.630
A small independent unit is camped nearby to resupply.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:52.120
Well, they won't be able to do a thing.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.830
Get us out there as soon as possible.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.390
Welcome back.

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:07.330
Any changes?

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.510
No, all is well.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.420
Where are Tanita and the others?

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.470
They have the supplies and are heading here.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.460
They should be here soon.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.220
I see.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.630
Once they're back, get things loaded as fast as you can.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:21.360
Yes, sir.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.970
We received word from Quasimodo.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:31.920
Did he say anything?

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.750
Nothing special.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.180
He said you met with him.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.940
Yes, it's been years.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:41.880
Really.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.570
I was worried as to what he'd been doing since he left the army,

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.440
but he seems as well as ever.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.890
Yeah, he hasn't changed.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.360
I want to know what the enemy is doing.

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:02.170
Get in touch with the battalion.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.400
Understood.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.610
Sister, what were you doing here?

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.050
Hey.

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:26.070
Everyone's back.

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:27.340
O-Okay.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.630
Hey, how was the spa?

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.750
Everything's here.

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.650
Good work.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:52.360
After this, we'll move to the Govitz Plains.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.030
There's been movement on the front lines,

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:57.140
and there may be a full-on attack soon.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.560
Understood.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.060
Okay, let's hurry.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.660
Right.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.940
Cargo from Ingelmia?

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:23.520
Yeah.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.750
That's why that ship was late.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.530
And that cargo was

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.220
industrial machine parts.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.030
They were taken to a nearby factory after unloading.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:40.360
The owner of the factory is named Gorgi.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.360
He's a famous Ingelmia sympathizer.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:44.660
I see.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.820
This is where it gets interesting.

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:50.220
Three of these "industrial machines" are scheduled

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.940
to be shipped out of Gorgi's factory tonight.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.930
They'll be passing through customs at 20:00 tonight.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.680
Terai.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.630
Get me Seeker.

00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:03.690
Yes, sir.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.670
I'll thank you the next time we meet.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.870
I hope you can do it before I get old.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:09.950
I can't guarantee that.

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:11.070
I've got Seeker.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.270
I'm done.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:40.730
Okay.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.550
Are you okay?

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:48.630
What do you mean?

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.070
Listen, you need to concentrate.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.330
Impulse antrieb status go.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:05.390
Sensor array activated.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.510
Environmental information integration confirmed.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:09.470
Weapon expansions online.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:11.420
Argevollen, all systems go!

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:20.870
That's right.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.440
Now's not the time.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.060
Now's not the time to think about my sister.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.030
Once we're this far,

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.980
all that's left is to stick our boot up their ass. Right, Bro?

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:51.960
Stop it, Thomas.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.950
Don't break radio silence if you don't have to.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:19.660
I made it in time.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.530
Sh-Shit!

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:56.630
A Trail Krieger!

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:58.390
That new model?

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:59.610
Here?

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.060
Tokimune, I commend you for slowing them down, if nothing else.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:13.580
She means everything else sucked, Tokimune-kun.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:14.820
I know that!

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:18.630
Contact HQ and tell them to delay the attack.

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:22.300
We will eliminate this obstacle and continue the operation.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.930
I won't let you stop us, new model.

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:44.020
Second Lieutenant, HQ has called off the attack!

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:45.730
They're ordering you to pull out.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.640
We can still continue the operation.

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.700
Tell that to HQ.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:57.790
I see.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:59.630
It's gotten faster,

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.870
but the pilot's skill hasn't improved at all.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:04.240
It's the machine's reaction systems.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.410
This is...

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:17.650
We've succeeded in our goal of stopping the surprise attack.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.940
There's no need to continue fighting.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.710
I'm not interesting in fighting,

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:29.640
but they sure are!

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.620
Bro, we're leaving, right?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.160
I can't leave the second lieutenant!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.870
Look at this.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.960
A battle is being held on the coast opposite Bellhals,

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.780
which is a neutral zone.

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:46.180
The coast is not a no-combat zone,

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:49.510
but there's no telling when the fight could spread to Bellhals.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.340
Is our beautiful city of Bellhals going to become a battlefield?

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:56.810
Our field marshal won't let that happen.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.980
Deploy the Sekiei where the bridge is in sight.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.670
If it comes down to it, we'll destroy the bridge.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:03.320
Yes, sir.

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.000
I lost him!

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.030
You're mine.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:38.230
I've got you!

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.460
Lorenz!

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:48.570
On it!

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:56.830
Thomas!

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:06.710
Ow...

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.080
C-Crap.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.830
How dare you kill Thomas?!

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.730
Damn it!

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:51.680
Tokimune is being pushed on the defensive.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.570
Silfy, help him.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:54.470
Roger.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:15.350
This is the end, Newtype.

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:34.620
What?

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.250
I'll do it!

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:45.700
Lieutenant!

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:54.470
Toulouse.

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:56.950
Get out of here, Second Lieutenant.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:57.850
But...

00:18:57.850 --> 00:18:58.950
Lieutenant!

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:19.890
I'm sorry.

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:25.250
Newtype...

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:29.070
Richthofen was the only one to make it out.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.260
Recover him.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.430
I'm going to go cool off a bit.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.660
The enemy movements on the Govitz Plains have stopped.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.780
There's been no change in the battlefield.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:53.980
Their sudden disadvantage caused them to call off the attack, I bet.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.760
We're that "disadvantage," aren't we?

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.580
Your intuition was right, wasn't it?

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.290
You said they were soldiers.

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:24.180
Who would've guessed they were Ingelmian soldiers?

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:28.690
Good work.

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:31.830
Oh... Thanks.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.900
That was amazing. Linkage Depth 17!

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:35.820
What's that?

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.970
The depth of your link with Argevollen.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:40.100
Didn't I tell you?

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:43.490
Isn't that like saying I got 17 points on a test?

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:44.710
That's amazing?

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.570
It's amazing for somebody who's only been piloting it for a few weeks.

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:50.090
Didn't it feel like it moved easier than before?

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:52.070
It might have...

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:54.120
Actually, today was the first time...

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.220
That I felt like I really fought.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:09.330
I destroyed the place you liked.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.710
Oh, come on. Don't worry about that.

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.650
It's actually more important to you, isn't it?

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.700
Since your sister was, well...

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:24.190
I'm going to do what I can for a while.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.070
I think there's some reason

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:31.110
that the place where my sister took her last picture

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:33.300
was where I was first able to really fight.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:37.340
Someday, I'll investigate what happened to my sister.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:39.090
I won't forget her.

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:40.650
But...

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.030
For now...

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:47.030
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.860
Promise
